.\" apfs-mount.1 - manual page for apfs-mount
.\" Generated for apfs-explorer project.
.TH APFS\-MOUNT 1 "2026-05-26" "apfs-explorer v1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
apfs\-mount \- mount APFS volumes on Windows via WinFsp
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B apfs\-mount
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.RB [ \-V | \-\-version ]
.I SUBCOMMAND
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.PP
Subcommands:
.PP
.B apfs\-mount mount
.RB [ \-d
.IR DEVICE ]
.RB [ \-v
.IR VOLUME ]
.RB [ \-l
.IR LETTER ]
.RB [ \-r ]
.PP
.B apfs\-mount snapshot
.RB { list | create | delete | revert }
.RB [ \-d
.IR DEVICE ]
.RB [ \-v
.IR VOLUME ]
.RB [ \-n
.IR NAME ]
.PP
.B apfs\-mount clone
.RB \-d
.IR DEVICE
.RB \-v
.IR VOLUME
.RB \-\-src
.IR PATH
.RB \-\-dst
.IR PATH
.PP
.B apfs\-mount volume
.RB { list | info }
.RB [ \-d
.IR DEVICE ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B apfs\-mount
mounts APFS-formatted volumes as Windows drive letters using the WinFsp user-mode
file system framework. It supports read and write access, snapshots, and
copy-on-write file cloning.
.PP
.B apfs\-mount
operates directly on block devices or disk image files. No kernel driver for the
APFS format is required; WinFsp provides the VFS bridge.
.PP
The tool runs on Windows 10 / Windows 11 (x86-64). WinFsp 2.1 or later must be
installed before use.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.SS mount
Mount an APFS volume as a Windows drive letter.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-device " " \fIDEVICE\fR
Block device or image file path. Examples:
.br
\fB\\\\\\\\.\\\\\\ PhysicalDrive1\fR (physical disk, requires elevation),
.br
\fBC:\\\\images\\\\disk.img\fR (image file).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-volume " " \fIVOLUME\fR
Volume name to mount. If omitted and only one APFS volume is present in the
container, that volume is selected automatically.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-letter " " \fILETTER\fR
Drive letter to assign (e.g.\& \fBZ\fR). If omitted, the next available letter
is assigned automatically.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-read\-only
Mount in read-only mode. Writes return \fBACCESS_DENIED\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-uid " " \fIUID\fR
Override the UID reported for all files (default: current user).
.TP
.BR \-\-gid " " \fIGID\fR
Override the GID reported for all files (default: current user primary group).
.SS snapshot
Manage APFS snapshots.
.TP
.B list
Print all snapshots in the named volume.
.TP
.B create
Create a new named snapshot of the current volume state. Requires \fB\-n\fR.
.TP
.B delete
Delete a named snapshot. Requires \fB\-n\fR.
.TP
.B revert
Revert the volume to a named snapshot. All data written after the snapshot is
.B permanently discarded.
Requires \fB\-n\fR.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-name " " \fINAME\fR
Snapshot name for create / delete / revert operations.
.SS clone
Create a copy-on-write clone of a file within a mounted volume. The clone
shares extents with the original until either is modified (reflink semantics).
.TP
.BR \-\-src " " \fIPATH\fR
Source file path (absolute APFS path, e.g.\& \fB/Users/alice/doc.pdf\fR).
.TP
.BR \-\-dst " " \fIPATH\fR
Destination file path for the clone.
.SS volume
Inspect APFS volumes in a container without mounting.
.TP
.B list
List all volumes in the container with name, role, and feature flags.
.TP
.B info
Print detailed information about a specific volume (use \fB\-v\fR to select).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-log\-level " " \fILEVEL\fR
Set log verbosity: \fBerror\fR, \fBwarn\fR, \fBinfo\fR (default), \fBdebug\fR, \fBtrace\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-log\-file " " \fIPATH\fR
Write log output to \fIPATH\fR in addition to stderr.
.SH EXAMPLES
Mount the first APFS volume on a physical disk as drive Z:
.PP
.RS
.nf
apfs\-mount mount \-d \\\\.\\PhysicalDrive1 \-l Z
.fi
.RE
.PP
Mount a specific volume from a disk image in read-only mode:
.PP
.RS
.nf
apfs\-mount mount \-d C:\\images\\backup.img \-v Macintosh\\ HD \-r
.fi
.RE
.PP
List all volumes in a disk image:
.PP
.RS
.nf
apfs\-mount volume list \-d C:\\images\\backup.img
.fi
.RE
.PP
List snapshots on a volume:
.PP
.RS
.nf
apfs\-mount snapshot list \-d \\\\.\\PhysicalDrive1 \-v Data
.fi
.RE
.PP
Create a snapshot named "before-update":
.PP
.RS
.nf
apfs\-mount snapshot create \-d \\\\.\\PhysicalDrive1 \-v Data \-n before\-update
.fi
.RE
.PP
Revert a volume to a snapshot (destructive):
.PP
.RS
.nf
apfs\-mount snapshot revert \-d \\\\.\\PhysicalDrive1 \-v Data \-n before\-update
.fi
.RE
.PP
Clone a file within a mounted APFS volume:
.PP
.RS
.nf
apfs\-mount clone \-d C:\\images\\disk.img \-v Data \\
    \-\-src /Users/alice/original.pdf \-\-dst /Users/alice/clone.pdf
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.B %PROGRAMDATA%\\apfs\-mount\\apfs\-mount.log
Default log file location when \fB\-\-log\-file\fR is not specified and logging
is directed to a file by the system tray wrapper.
.TP
.B %LOCALAPPDATA%\\apfs\-mount\\config.toml
Optional user configuration file. Overrides compiled-in defaults.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
General error (bad arguments, device not found, etc.). Error details on stderr.
.TP
.B 2
Mount failed (WinFsp error, volume unreadable, or encrypted volume).
.TP
.B 3
Snapshot operation failed (name conflict, volume has no snapshot support, etc.).
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Enable debug logging with \fB\-\-log\-level debug\fR to trace B-tree lookups,
block allocations, and WinFsp callbacks.
.PP
Encrypted volumes are detected at open time and rejected with a clear error
message rather than returning corrupt data.
.SH AUTHORS
apfs-explorer contributors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR winfsp (1),
.BR diskutil (8)
.PP
APFS specification: Apple File System Reference (developer.apple.com/support/downloads).
.PP
